# SSC requires package files to be plain ASCII with LF line endings, and
# tools/make_ssc_bundle.py asserts exactly that before it will build the zip.
# core.autocrlf is on for this checkout, so without these rules a fresh clone
# would hand every .sthlp back with CRLF endings and the bundle build would
# fail (or, worse, ship CRLF files to the archive). Pin them to LF everywhere.
*.sthlp text eol=lf
*.pkg   text eol=lf
*.toc   text eol=lf
*.do    text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
LICENSE text eol=lf

# Stata datasets are binary; never line-ending-convert or try to diff them
*.dta binary
